course: dictionary
lesson: 14624
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words can mean different things. Possessed is one of them. Its meaning depends on the words around it, so check the context before you decide. «Mum possessed a red bicycle when she was little.» Possessed means had or owned.
explain: In a ghost story, possessed means controlled by an evil spirit. «The old mill was possessed, the villagers whispered.» The clues are ghost, old and whispered. The mill is not owned by anyone here; something evil has taken it over.
explain: Possessed can also show a very strong feeling. «Jake cleaned his room like a boy possessed.» Jake is not under a spell. He is working with wild energy. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap in your meaning to check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: In old, formal writing, possessed of means having a quality. «She was possessed of great courage.» This means she had great courage. If you are not sure, swap in had or owned and see if it fits.
fact: Possessed is the past form of the verb possess, which means to have or own.
fact: «Possessed» can mean controlled by an evil spirit, as in ghost stories.
fact: «Like a man possessed» means doing something with wild, fierce energy.
fact: «Possessed of» is formal and old-fashioned, and it means having a quality.
fact: In a maths problem, «Tom possessed 15 cards» simply means Tom had 15 cards.
exercise: «Tom possessed 15 cards.» What does possessed mean here? | *Had | Threw away | Lost them all | Was haunted by a ghost
exercise: «The villagers said the old mill was possessed.» What does possessed mean in this ghost story? | Painted bright blue | Sold to a farmer | Had lots of windows | *Controlled by an evil spirit
exercise: «Jake cleaned his room like a boy possessed.» What does like a boy possessed suggest? | Carefully, one toy at a time | Very sleepy and slow | Without any energy at all | *With wild, fierce energy
test: «The queen possessed many jewels and gold coins.» What does possessed mean here? | Sold | Lost | Hid | *Owned
test: «She was possessed of great courage.» What does possessed of mean? | Lost her courage | *Having great courage | Afraid of courage | Chased by courage
exam: Which meaning fits best in «The room was possessed by a cold, angry spirit»? | Full of toys | *Controlled by an evil spirit | Very clean and tidy | Painted in bright colours
